# The public API of the store as the gateway exposes it (VS Code REST Client / Rider .http).
# Every request goes through the gateway; the services are not reachable from outside.
# Errors are RFC 9457 problems (application/problem+json): 401/403 for the caller, 404 for a
# missing resource, 409 for a state conflict, 422 for request content a rule rejects.
#
# Environment: local compose or "dotnet run" of the gateway on port 5000. Sign in first
# (login or a demo login), then paste the accessToken into @token. The refresh token arrives
# in an httpOnly cookie (store_refresh, path /api/v1/auth); access tokens last 15 minutes.

@gateway = http://localhost:5000
@api = {{gateway}}/api/v1
@token = paste-an-access-token-here
@idempotencyKey = {{$guid}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- auth

### Register (409 when the e-mail is taken, 422 when the password is too weak)
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "buyer@example.test",
  "password": "Buyer-Password-1!",
  "confirmPassword": "Buyer-Password-1!",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Buyer"
}

### Login (401 for wrong credentials, 423 while the account is locked)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "buyer@example.test",
  "password": "Buyer-Password-1!"
}

### Demo customer, no password
POST {{api}}/auth/demo-login

### Demo administrator (read-only admin panel), no password
POST {{api}}/auth/demo-admin-login

### The signed-in user's profile (204 without a token)
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Store the delivery address in the profile (an empty value clears it)
PUT {{api}}/auth/me/address
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "simpleAddress": "1 Example Street, Example City"
}

### A new access token for the session in the refresh cookie (rotated on every call; the REST
### Client keeps the cookie from the sign-in above). 401 for a spent, expired or missing cookie.
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh

### Logout: revokes the session behind the refresh cookie and removes the cookie
POST {{api}}/auth/logout

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- catalogue (public)

### A page of active products; every filter is optional
GET {{api}}/products?page=1&pageSize=12&search=&group=all&category=all&company=all&colors=black&order=low&price=100,900&sale=true

### One product (404 for an unknown or deleted id)
GET {{api}}/products/1

### The values the catalogue can be filtered by
GET {{api}}/products/meta

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- catalogue (administrators)

### Every product, inactive ones included (any admin)
GET {{api}}/products/admin?page=1&pageSize=50&sortBy=price&sortDir=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a product (true-admin only; demo-admin gets 403)
POST {{api}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Example armchair",
  "description": "An armchair created from the .http file to exercise the write path.",
  "price": 499.99,
  "salePrice": 449.99,
  "category": "chairs",
  "company": "luxora",
  "newArrival": true,
  "image": "https://example.test/armchair.jpg",
  "colors": ["black", "gray"],
  "groups": ["furniture"],
  "materials": ["oak", "linen"],
  "widthCm": 80
}

### Partial update: absent fields keep their value, null clears an optional one; isActive:true restores a deleted product
PUT {{api}}/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "salePrice": null,
  "isActive": true
}

### Delete = hide from the public catalogue (the row stays for past orders)
DELETE {{api}}/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- cart (signed-in customer)

### The cart with today's prices (priceChanged tells whether a line was refreshed)
GET {{api}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a line; the same product and colour again raises the quantity (422 for an unknown product)
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 2,
  "color": "black"
}

### Change a line (404 for a line that is not in this cart)
PUT {{api}}/cart/items/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 3
}

### Remove a line
DELETE {{api}}/cart/items/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Merge a guest cart into the server cart at sign-in
POST {{api}}/cart/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": 2, "quantity": 1, "color": "white" }
  ]
}

### Pieces in the cart / sum of the lines
GET {{api}}/cart/count
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{api}}/cart/total
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Empty the cart
DELETE {{api}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- orders (signed-in customer)

### Place an order from the cart. Re-send with the same Idempotency-Key to get the same order back
### (422 for an empty cart or a reused key with a different body, 409 for a product that left the catalogue)
POST {{api}}/orders/from-cart
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "userEmail": "buyer@example.test",
  "customerName": "Test Buyer",
  "deliveryAddress": "1 Example Street, Example City",
  "notes": null,
  "saveAddress": true
}

### One order: the customer's own (403 for somebody else's), any order for an administrator
GET {{api}}/orders/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The customer's orders, newest first
GET {{api}}/orders/my-orders?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Whether the customer ordered before (the first order is discounted)
GET {{api}}/orders/has-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The rules an order is priced by, for the cart page (public)
GET {{api}}/orders/pricing-rules

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- admin panel (demo-admin sees masked customer data)

### All orders
GET {{api}}/admin/orders?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Orders of one customer
GET {{api}}/admin/orders/by-user/{{userId}}?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One order
GET {{api}}/admin/orders/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Orders and revenue per day, week and product over the last N days
GET {{api}}/admin/orders/stats?days=30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Accounts, filtered by a fragment of the e-mail or name and by activity
GET {{api}}/admin/users?search=&isActive=true&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One account
GET {{api}}/admin/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- audit trail (administrators)

### Entries newest first; every filter is optional, from/to are ISO 8601 instants
GET {{api}}/auditlog?entityName=Order&entityId=1&userId=&from=2026-09-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-12-31T23:59:59Z&page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One entry
GET {{api}}/auditlog/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- health (each host)

### Liveness / readiness of the gateway; the services answer the same paths on their own ports
GET {{gateway}}/health/live

###
GET {{gateway}}/health/ready
